# remember — success
#
# REMEMBER exists only in the childhood-reminescence phase, so this test is the one that must NOT
# pass --skip-childhood: that flag skips the phase entirely and fills the starting kit as if it had
# run. Every other script in the suite passes it, which is why this verb had no test.
#
# The childhood is the first screen of a run and is played in the dark: no sky, no world, no card,
# no header, no status row. It opens on ONE symbol, whoever is remembering. Looking at it says what
# has been lost — who they are — and discloses the fragments of the first memory, unnamed until one
# is looked at ("observe · a memory"). A fragment is looked at, thought about, and reached for; the
# next memory's fragments then hang from the fragment just remembered, so the whole childhood grows
# as one tree. What is behind is a record: its texts can be read, nothing of it answers a click.
# No will is asked to look or to think here.
#
# The phase auto-succeeds by design — no plausibility check, no noetic cost, difficulty 0, so no
# dice. There is no `strategy` here and no meaningful failure case; `cli/remember/` has one script,
# deliberately. The fragment is named: --seed 42 fixes which memory comes first and what it holds.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue

# The phase opens on its own — no travel, no location. Wait for the mode rather than for idleness.
wait mode ChildhoodReminescence 60
advance 12 180

# --- one symbol in the dark, and nothing else on the screen ---
expect-not ???
expect-not NOETIC
expect-not Under the Tree
expect-no-state trees element
expect-state symbols click observe person in "Under the Tree" x1
expect-no-state symbols click observe thing
point observe person
wait 1
expect-state pointer-label ground=yellow text=observe · myself

# --- looking at it: what has been lost, and the first memory's fragments ---
click observe person
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
expect-state trees element "Myself"
expect-state texts I have forgotten who I am
expect-no-state symbols click observe person
expect-state symbols click observe "a scream" in "Myself"
point observe "a scream"
wait 1
expect-state pointer-label ground=yellow text=observe · a memory

# --- a second fragment looked at and thought about, which will not be the one remembered ---
click observe "a whisper"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click think "a whisper"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
expect-state trees act state=waiting verb=remember

click observe "a scream"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click think "a scream"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180

click act scream
advance 12 180

# No dice: the result is up at once.
expect SUCCESS
expect-verb remember

# Its CONTINUE moves on to the next memory — and the tree stays: the new fragments hang from the
# fragment just remembered.
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-state trees element "Myself"
expect-state trees element "a scream"
expect-state trees element "a whisper"
expect-state symbols click observe "manure smelt" in "a scream"
# ...unnamed like the first ones, until one is looked at.
point observe "manure smelt"
wait 1
expect-state pointer-label ground=yellow text=observe · a memory

# --- what is behind is a record: no fragment of the first memory is offered, the act that was
# --- waiting on the other one has lapsed, and nothing is thought about either ---
expect-no-state symbols in "Myself"
expect-no-state symbols click think
expect-no-state symbols click act
expect-state trees act state=lapsed verb=remember
expect-no-state trees act state=waiting

# --- and its texts are still there to be read ---
expect-state texts I have forgotten who I am
quit
